What the MIT licence does not cover
===================================

The MIT licence in `LICENSE` covers the source code, the prompt and the
documentation written for this project. It covers neither of the following.

Article texts
-------------

`data/`, `reference/` and `src/lib/content/` hold texts published by kremlin.ru
and their official English translations. They are the property of the
Presidential Administration of Russia, are included here only as the input and
the output of the extraction pipeline, and are not licensed by `LICENSE`. Read
them at their source, which each dump records in its own header.

Grammeme names
--------------

The tag table in `src/lib/grammar.ts` is derived from the OpenCorpora dictionary
(http://opencorpora.org, CC BY-SA) through pymorphy3-dicts
(https://github.com/no-plagiarism/pymorphy3-dicts, MIT, © Danylo Halaiko). That
table remains under CC BY-SA, with attribution to OpenCorpora.
